# The plugin manager's Exercise, the owner's request of 2026-10-04: a test for each working
# plugin that starts the planner, opens the manager with Ctrl+P - the PLUGINS tab, by the owner's
# word - (MainV2.ProcessCmdKey,
# MainV2.cs:4118-4122), finds the plugin's row - loaded, enabled, green - and tries it: its Try
# lists what it added to the maps' menus, and a click on one runs it as the map's menu would.
# The config holds `tabcontrolactions`, so the Drone ID plugin's message does not show at start.
# And an empty `DisabledPlugins`: every plugin on, Open Drone ID too, which is off until a user
# turns it on (the owner, 2026-10-05).
#
# MapIconDesc (mapicondesc.wasm): Change icon Description asks what the vehicle's map icon should
# show; answered, the box closes.
# The built-in plugins: the runner leaves them out unless a script asks for them.
env MP_BUILTIN_PLUGINS 1
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 10
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
setup printf '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><Config><tabcontrolactions>tabQuick;</tabcontrolactions><DisabledPlugins></DisabledPlugins></Config>' > "$WORK/config.xml"
expect plugins.MapIconDesc.state running
expect plugins.question none
key ctrl+p
expect screen plugins
expect plugin-manager.row.3 MapIconDesc|mapicondesc.wasm|enabled|green
click plugin-manager-try-3
expect plugin-manager.exercising MapIconDesc
expect plugin-manager.exercise.entries Change icon Description
click plugin-manager-run-4-0
expect plugins.question ~ What do you want it to show?
type tested
key Return
expect plugins.question none
